cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "casgf: Green's functions and topological winding numbers from CASSCF active spaces"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Xie
    given-names: Ziren
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/xieziren/casgf"
abstract: >-
  Computes one-particle Green's functions of CASSCF active spaces by full
  diagonalisation of the N and N+-1 particle-number sectors, assembled into a
  Lehmann representation. Provides spectral functions, maps of the poles and
  zeros of det G, orbital-symmetry blocking, and topological winding numbers
  evaluated on closed contours in the complex frequency plane. Built on PySCF
  and NumPy, with no compiled dependencies.
keywords:
  - quantum chemistry
  - CASSCF
  - Green's function
  - exact diagonalisation
  - spectral function
  - topological invariant
  - winding number
